Z||000008||Formula88||12-06-2001||09:05 PM||||Sorry, Archie, I don't like it.  I don't care for the dash overlay type of dashboards.  If it's keeping the original dash, I'd go with the original dash.  To me, if I'm doing a dash replacement, I want a totally different look, kinda like Pisa's Euro dash (only as an example).  <P>Something with more of a Ferrari look to it.<P>Can't wait to see what else you're cooking up, though!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||12-06-2001||09:07 PM||||Hi Archie, I like it allright, but I would switch the speakers to take component style drivers (say 5-6" and a 1.5" tweter or so)<P>Also, how about ditching the crappy air vents and glassing over the same area and including some *nice* new circuliar vents?<P>Glove box? (assume you're adding one later)<P>mmm searches for posts by archie....<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||Cheever3000||12-06-2001||10:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>if I'm doing a dash replacement, I want a totally different look</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Same here.  That's interesting, and I'm sure a lot of work.  Please include in your time estimates a consideration for removal of the <I>old</I> dash, because I've never done it and it could take me hours if not days.  Please keep working on the idea, but the price would have to be much lower to fit my meager budget.  Oh, and a cupholder would get you many, many customers, guaranteed!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Archie||12-06-2001||11:06 PM||||This is great, thanks for the input and please keep it coming.<P>You know, this is pretty interesting. A supplier like me starts to design something and if people don't like it, no matter how well intentioned the design is, it's all a waste of time & $$$ if no one buys it. I originally set out to come up with an inexpensive dash (&lt;$600), that would be an easy install (10 minutes Max), a dash that would be 100% complete when you opened the box & use all the original Fiero gages. <P>I've seen the complaints about super expensive interiors, that were too difficult to install & that were incomplete and needed a big checkbook to complete. I thought there was a demand for an inexpensive, complete, easy to install alternative for Fiero owners that want something different that they can afford. I still think there is a demand, but considering the cost to develope something to this point. I don't know if it's worth trying again. I would think that there would be a demand for plug and play dash and I think that I might go ahead and continue developement of this one a little more yet.<P>I have a couple of other designs that would be much more expensive but I don't think people want to spend a couple grand to ave an interior that is too hard to install and compete correctly.<P>Thanks for the input and please keep it coming.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000012||stingant0||12-06-2001||11:21 PM||||It looks pretty good. But you MISSED something Archie..CUP HOLDERS. That is the one thing that I wish I had. <P>BTW...do you use the getrag with your conversions...if so any mods done...i need to know this for my dohc swap.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Archie||12-06-2001||11:34 PM||||nevermind<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Sage||12-06-2001||11:40 PM||||Archie:<P>You could have called this thread, "Plug for a plug"!  Looks good.  Is this going to be a slip on cover, or a dash replacement?  Since you are incorporating an actual glove box, you could put cup holders on the inside of the glove box door!  How about an included panel(could be an option) for auxiliary gauges?  Is it going to include control switches, or will the stock ones be used?  <P>Like to see one covered and installed, before coming to any final conclusions, but it looks very promising!  <P>Keep us posted on the progress.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000015||cadaver||12-07-2001||12:15 AM||||You keep calling it a "dash" when its just a "cover"||||reg||1
Z||000016||Archie||12-07-2001||12:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B>You keep calling it a "dash" when its just a "cover"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow, can't fool you can we?<P>Looks like you may have discovered a major fraud as it's taking place.<P>How about if I call it a Dash after the cover is put on?<P>I thought it was pretty obvious that this was a cover that fit over the original dash in an attempt to partially disguise the original Fiero "Look".<P>I wear a hat, but it's really just a cover.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Nashco||12-07-2001||03:24 AM||||LOL..anyway...<P>Just a few thoughts/suggestions.  I see the cover doesn't deal with one of the things I see complained about MOST often...broken lower corners.  Any thoughts of making the cover wrap around the corners?  This may be easiest to deal with if you maybe think something up like Artherd suggested about using round vents.  You may be able to make a new vent (vent cover for those who choose to call them so) that is included in the new dash piece.<P>Also, if this is going to cover so much, why not a little more and cover the stock heater panel/stereo panel wrap around?  Most people that are looking for the cheap and easy cover have also not spent the time or money to replace the curling edges on their interior, and this would be one more reason for them to cheap out and not buy that part or fix it.<P>Ok, those were my suggestions..now my opinion <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I personally don't care much for the looks.  I think this is mainly because (due to its "cover" action) it looks boxy just like the stock dash, and it retains the stock speaker grills, which look somewhat out of place IMO.  Some may like it, but personally I wouldn't buy it.  Then again, I'm a do-it-yourself by nature, so I probably wouldn't anyway.  I really don't think my opinion should mean much because of this, but you may think a little on the suggestions above.<P>Thanks for doing what you do, and doing it well Archie! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||revin||12-07-2001||07:35 AM||||Archie,<BR>Please don't hate, I don't think it is too much of a radical change for me to get right now. Seems that if they made a dash cover(out of material) it would look similar to the one you fashioned. sorry. I would have added some gauge pods to the design. I do see the hole where the org. gauges are, but add some angled gauge pods there. <BR>I would like to get one like some of the kit cars offer without the price. Maybe a cheaper knock-off with some of the options others described in this thread.<BR>I am in no way a designer,just a thinker.(like how about adding a rear view mirror, like on some Le Maunds racers. up on the roof just in front of the sunroof. OR a one piece rear end that will flip up to service some of those hot V8's easier?<BR>Sorry just my thoughts.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Revin||||reg||1
Z||000019||Sage||12-07-2001||08:05 AM||||Archie:<P>No flames here, just trying to communicate.<P>Nobody appreciates more than me the time effort, money and energy that goes into developing a new part.  <P>That said, I think the presentation was a little misleading. People more than likely figured that if YOU were going to bother making a replacement for the stock Fiero dash, it would be that: a REPLACEMENT, not a slip cover.  The amount of work that you put into the v8 conversions leads people to believe you don't mess around!  The original pics look like it's in there for trial fitting, showing what it would look like in raw form.  Also, I don't think anyone would guess that a slip on cover would bring a $600 ticket either!  Yea, it should have been fairly obvious that you can't swap out a dash in 10 minutes, but for $600 I think people expect more than just a "cover"!  On the other hand, the body on these cars is "just a cover" and what does a rebody kit bring?  Big bucks!  The difference is the origianl gets replaced, not just covered up.  I understand about needing to get paid for r&d and the labor for production, but $600?  This may be a viable project, but in order for it to meet your expectations in sales response, I think you will have to narrow the profit margin.  Nashco brought up a good point also, the bottoms of the vent openings.   The "cover" should be made to cover these, even if it were seperate pieces that came up from the bottom and attached to the top.  Making it include the radio/ heater surround is also a good suggestion.<P>You asked what we thought, these are just some of mine.<P>Anyway, keep up the good work and good luck with the project!<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Archie||12-07-2001||11:27 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sage:<BR><B>Archie:<P>You can read the rest of Sage's comments above.... <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've looked back over my comments in the thread so far, and I've never said that this was a replacement dash. Anyone looking at the original pictures should have been able to tell that is was a cover to fit over the original dash. Anyone following this thread to this point who thinks that this was to be a replacement dash is jumping to conclusions because it was never presented to you as such.<P>I said the price would be &lt;$600 (Less Than $600).<P>I also said that Mr. Mike would be doing the covers. Considering what he gets for the leather seat covers, the final price would depend a lot on what he charges for the covers once they have been designed & completed.<P>Yes, when Mr. Mike designs the patterns for the cover we were going to have sufficient material to wrap around, tuck in and cover the area under the vents.<P>As far as "dash Covers" as opposed to "Dash Replacements" are concerned, I think you should look at all the other dash kits that are available. If you look at them, you'll see that nearly EVERYONE of them is actually a "cover" they all retain the original Fiero base dashboard because it includes defroster and A/C venting ductwork. Even the PISA wrap around dash still has the base Fiero dash underneath it. If someone was to design a Total Replacement Dash the cost and complexity of installation would make it so expensive that most people wouldn't be able to afford it. I remember the Pirana dash (from Carlisle a few years ago) that everyone, including myself, loved. Yeah they all loved it until they found out the guy wanted more than $6K for it.<P>Now, a lot of people think that the modular design of the Fiero dash is a problem. I would think that a "Slip Cover" that eliminates the "Modular" look at an affordable price & easily installed would be something that some Fiero owners would consider.<P>When I got to the shop this AM, I took another look at the "slip cover" and I think it looks a lot better in person than in the pics. & I can imagine what it will look like with the nice high quality cover on it. (Mr. Mike is known for the quality of his work) I will be continuing with the developement on this and a couple other "slip covers" I've been working on. <P>Anyway, thanks for your input.<P>Archie<P>BTW, can you tell that I don't like the term "Slip Cover"?<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||MinnGreenGT||12-07-2001||11:53 AM||||I officially withold any opinions until I see a completed picture.  I've seen many projects that, while in production stage, look just shotty (not that it does, mind you).  I can usually visualize what exterior body parts look like before completion (photoshop helps with that too).  But an interior make look strange right up until the point of completion- and they usually do.<P>Archie- I look forward to seeing your finished dash.  <P><FONT SIZE="1">btw: there's another question for you in my other thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016105.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016105.html</A>  thanks!</FONT><P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Sage||12-07-2001||12:06 PM||||Allrighty then!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> Good points...all.  I think I can "see" the finished product too, and my opinion is, that it would be a very nice, welcome improvement on the factory set up.  Maybe $500-$600 would be a realistic price, I figure that it will probably just cover the amount of labor and materials that will go into producing one for shipment, but allot of the people on this forum didn't pay a whole lot more than that for thier whole car!  I think there will be a market for this item, but it will be the high end market, and most of the folks in that bracket really expect perfection,(sometimes unrealistically).  Like I said, I wasn't running the project down, just expressing some thoughts that occured, which is what you asked for, right?<P><BR>Mr. Mikes' stuff is NOT cheap and I'm sure it will give a very rich look to the finished product. Will there be any padding under the leather? We all know that when you do anything, it gets done right, so I think everyone should reserve judgement, till the finished product is unvieled and the final price revealed.<P>There is no doubt in my mind that the pics are not a fair representation of the effect actually achieved by the install, but it's what we had to look at and go on to provide input.<P>Still think you should make it come down to include the heater radio surround.  As for the dash corners, good deal, it will provide an effective, easy solution for the broken stock ones!<P>Let's wait and see the finished product, I know it's gonna be a gas!<P>Sorry for the "slip cover" referance, I just figured it would get a rise out of you! <P> Don't you feel more energetic this morning now?  LOL  (I know, I got a warped sense of humor!)<P>Peace.<P>Keep up the good work.<P><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000023||Mr.Frosty||12-07-2001||12:12 PM||||Wow,That's some harsh stuff everybody.Archie,I personally like it,and the fact that it's going to be covered by Mr.Mike makes it even better.I think it is a "BIG" improvement over stock.It gets rid of that "Pod" look to the instrument cluster.I don't care if it's a "cover" or not,if it looks cleaner and more modern than the original,then right on.The price isn't bad either;it's a helluva lot less than anything else out there.Keep up the good work Archie,you have a future customer.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000024||Butter||12-07-2001||12:30 PM||||Archie,<BR>Neat Idea!  I think I understand what your getting at as a cover to change apperance and hide the modular look with quick installation time.  This would limit some of the versatillity that one would get with a dash replacement.  <P>My questions are 1. can the area above the center console be used to mount aftermarket guages inside easily?  2. Is the glove compartment going to be open or will it be closeable?  3. After installation will it be just as easy to remove in order to facilitate maintenence for dash components or changes?  4. Does the cover include covers for the speaker grills?  Mine are nasty.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buttersig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||StuGood||12-07-2001||12:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>This is great, thanks for the input and please keep it coming...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I admire your thick skinned-ness (a little-known word I just made up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  Not everyone is so willing to accept honest critcism for their creations.<P>Blame my lack of imagination, but I think I just have a hard time getting past the stark white color of the prototype.  I bet it looks way better, when it's color-matched to the rest of the dash.    <P>Maybe the $600 price seems a lot to sink into one car, but maybe not if you think: "leather dash."  Would the new dash be transferrable to another Fiero, if one decided to sell / move up/ change style?  Is it a (roughly) 10-minute job to take it out, also?  I'm guessing that more than one set of Mr. Mike's seats have been swapped prior to putting a Fiero for sale.<P>Just my thoughts, for what they're worth...<P>   ||||reg||14
Z||000026||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||12-07-2001||03:56 PM||||I personally like the minimal use of material and interior volume theme of the Fiero. It keeps it in line with the racecar-out-of-the-box philosophy. Your prototype is good, but its shape and resultant quality of finish (courtesy of Mr.Mike's)may contrast a smidge too starkly with the radio and center console's abhorrant styling and finish. <BR>I do think it is a bit too early to critique it though. It needs to go through the asthetic phase of development. It is, after all, a cosmetic accessory for the car. I am eager to see how it melds synergistically with the overall Gestalt of the Fiero interior styling paradigm...<BR>Stop me before I sound any more pretentious than I already do! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>my cat's sitting in my scrambled eggs.||||reg||1
Z||000027||MinnGreenGT||12-07-2001||04:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ali_Gulf_Fiero:<BR><B>...abhorrant... melds synergistically... overall Gestalt... paradigm...<P>Stop me before I sound any more pretentious than I already do!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm... just wondering if you tried to run the spell-check?  It might get confused  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> J/K||||reg||1
