Z||000029||Jake_Dragon||12-07-2001||06:21 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2_2.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1_1.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CHSpiff_1.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">                <BR>                    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||72vinman||12-07-2001||09:39 PM||||Archie, Please keep in mind that many of us are not as handy as we would like to be. The fact that it slips over the existing dash quite easily seems to be a key feature for me. Some of us need quick and easy. For this I thank you. It looks much more modern and think it would look great in black leather with my carbon fiber dash surrounds.<BR>Can't wait to see a completed prototype <BR>One small problem $$$$<BR>$600 US is about $950 Canadian that does not include shipping and duties.<BR>Keep up the good work and please keep us advised of any updates.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000031||theogre||12-08-2001||12:18 AM||||Well..... you asked.....<P>I think it's off to an interesting start.<P>I'd like to see a little better treatment of the side air outlets and the center pod. The integration of the master gauge cluster is nice. How are you going to accomodate the aux gauge pod on the center pod?<P>As a cover your ass thing.... there's a link in my cave to the FMVSS standards. There are standards for the dash in there. You might want to give them a read. They can help you avoid compliance problems and they may give some insite on other things.<P>Would an Ogre buy this? hard to say. Not having a glove box really isn't a problem to me. I was able to add the horizontal pocket when I replaced the dash last year. It's way better than the sideways pocket some jackass at gm/pontiac shoved in them. My first reaction on that, way back in 86, was "what the hell is that supposed to be?" Even with the horizontal one, I hardly put anything in it. The console pocket over the ECM holds the stuff I need it to.... the lug lock, tire guage, registration and insurance cards, impliment of scratching (pen), shooting glasses (really handy in heavy fog, try them. beats fog lights.), a few (large handfull of) napkins.....<P>I'd also recomend you see what the alteration does to the defoger outlets. The side ones really do work. (as small as they are they do work.) the center one is already kind of slow because most of it blows straight up. would be nice if part of it was diverted to the sides of the windscreen.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000032||fotofrank||12-08-2001||01:05 AM||||Archie, sorry to say I got one simmilar to your design from PISA a while back. The PISA one comes eather brown or black and is covered in a "leather" type material. I don't remember what the cost was but they are on the PISA web site and also in the Big Fiero Book. The down side to the PISA cover is a glove box must also be purchased to complete the job. I feel that the look it gives modernizes the interior.  Maybe if you changed some stuff, like adding cup holders <BR>(pop out? or mayby fold down- may take less room in the cover when not in use) and include the glove box.Also a provision for rally gauges. Offering different color covers can also be a draw. To be different a small digital clock added to the dash cover would be nice. Off course all this takes money. How about some cheep inside door panels to match the dash cover? I belive PISA wants $500.00 for theirs. Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE||||reg||9
Z||000033||dourain86gt||12-08-2001||02:47 AM||||Hey archie it's not bad but have you seen this thread on an interior upgrade?<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012320.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012320.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000034||dourain86gt||12-08-2001||02:50 AM||||In my humble opinion that interior would be the ideal interior for your Finale/Fino Kit.(which by the way I am trying to save up for and buy! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012320.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012320.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000035||Cozmo||12-08-2001||10:50 AM||||Whatta guy!<BR>You identified a need and came up with a viable solution...<BR>The fact that you and Mr. Mike are involved means that the final product WILL be produced (as opposed to a lot of "vaporware" products touted on this Forum) AND will be of excellent quality and value.<BR>As far as suggestions and "constructive criticism", I understand the fine line you have to walk in designing a drop in non-destructive dash.<BR>Areas I think all of us would agree need to be addressed are:<BR>Dash corners... sounds like you have this "covered" <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Warped vinyl... maybe play around with how your dash fits over the center console area to cover more of the pod.<BR>Speaker area... maybe integrate a generic speaker grille into your dash right over the existing speaker cutout. That lets the customer have more options in speaker selection.<BR>Glove box...  It would be nice to have something more practical than the factory one. Looking at your setup, there is room for a number of configurations.<BR>In spite of the lukewarm comments made here so far, I think you have a really great concept percolating. This dash, in combination with Mr. Mikes' seats will improve the looks and feel of a Fiero (as well as adding that "leather smell") and if you come up with some conceptually similar door panels eventually you can re-do the whole interior easily and inexpensively.<BR>I think around $600 is a fair price.<BR>I can't wait to see one with leather on it...<BR>It should be awesome!<BR>Kudos, Archie...don't let the nitpickers get to you...<P><BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Cardone</B><BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thankssig.jpg">   <BR><B>'85 2M6 SE Targa</B>||||reg||1
Z||000036||Fierowrecker||12-08-2001||11:55 AM||||Hey Archie!<BR>I think it looks good!<BR>Will it come off as easilly as it goes on?<BR>&lt;$600 sounds good for a new interior look, especially if you don't want to look like a Fiero inerior, with a body kit...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
